# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the CareerAI India React + Vite project.

## What Was Done

### 1. Fetched Latest Documentation
Retrieved the official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart guide from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart to ensure we followed the most up-to-date installation instructions.

### 2. Installed Package
- Added `@vercel/speed-insights` package (version ^2.0.0) to dependencies
- Used npm to install the package in the careerai-india directory
- Updated package-lock.json for dependency consistency

### 3. Integrated SpeedInsights Component
Modified `/src/main.jsx`:
- Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/react'`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component alongside the existing `<Analytics />` component
- Placed inside the `<StrictMode>` wrapper as per React best practices

### 4. Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully (vite build)
- ✅ No new linting errors introduced
- ✅ Package.json and lock file properly updated

## Modified Files
- `/careerai-india/package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `/careerai-india/package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and dependencies
- `/careerai-india/src/main.jsx` - Added SpeedInsights component import and usage

## Implementation Details
Following the official Vercel documentation for React applications, the SpeedInsights component was added to the root render location (main.jsx) where it will automatically:
- Track Core Web Vitals (CLS, FID, LCP, FCP, TTFB, INP)
- Send performance metrics to Vercel when the app is deployed
- Work alongside the existing Vercel Analytics integration

## Next Steps
To enable Speed Insights:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Navigate to Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard
3. Click "Enable" to activate the feature
4. The tracking will begin collecting performance data automatically

## Notes
- The implementation follows React framework-specific instructions from the official docs
- SpeedInsights component is lightweight and won't impact application performance
- Works seamlessly with the existing @vercel/analytics integration already in the project
- Pre-existing linting error in App.jsx (unused 'dash' variable) is unrelated to this implementation
